1
00:00:07.148 --> 00:00:13.148
This is your dashboard on day one. The
checklist at the top is your to-do list.

2
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:20.830
Every amber row is something not set up
yet — and each one has a shortcut link.

3
00:00:20.844 --> 00:00:24.844
Let's start with the big one: putting a
tenant on a lease.

4
00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:31.078
Name, unit, rent, lease start. That's all
the app needs to start tracking.

5
00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:46.029
Saved. The unit is now occupied and rent
is expected every month.

6
00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:51.174
Every tenant gets a portal link — no
password, no app to install.

7
00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:59.623
Share this on WhatsApp or email. Tenants
see their balance, invoices and documents

8
00:00:59.623 --> 00:01:01.123
here.

9
00:01:04.441 --> 00:01:08.214
When rent lands in your account, record it
here. Pick the tenant, enter the amount,

10
00:01:08.214 --> 00:01:09.714
done.

11
00:01:12.556 --> 00:01:18.556
The app now knows what you expected and
what actually arrived.

12
00:01:35.947 --> 00:01:39.618
Spending works the same way. Category,
amount, save — that's your P&L building

13
00:01:39.618 --> 00:01:41.118
itself.

14
00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:57.609
Back on the dashboard, the checklist has
caught up. Green rows mean the app can

15
00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:59.109
stop nagging.

16
00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:04.867
From here everything updates itself —
arrears, occupancy, cash flow.

17
00:02:05.134 --> 00:02:10.134
Finish the remaining rows when you have
five minutes. It's worth it.

18
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:14.150
Next up: getting your existing records in
— Bulk import without duplicates.
